{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_sub_valueRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_sub_valueRatio","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L107-L117","doc":"The value-ratio and the symmetry constant differ by exactly\n`S₂₁ / S₁₁` — so they agree iff the off-diagonal `S₂₁` vanishes. At the\n4₁ substrate `S₂₁ = −0.3022 ≠ 0`, which is the whole gap between R2's\n3.7067 and R3's exact 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.rawEntry_eq_symmetryConstant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.rawEntry_eq_symmetryConstant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L94-L105","doc":"**Separation criterion.** Away from the base point the raw entry and the\nsymmetry constant are the *same* number precisely when\n`S₁₂ + S₂₁ = S₁₂ · S₁₁`; otherwise they are genuinely different objects.\n(For the 4₁ substrate data the right side fails, and the two readings are\n1.5852 vs 3.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.readings_coincide_at_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.readings_coincide_at_base","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L82-L92","doc":"**The `q → 0` degeneracy.** At a base point where `S₁₁ = 1` and\n`S₂₁ = 0` — exactly GGM eq (60)'s `S⁺(0) = [[1,3],[0,1]]` — all three\nreadings collapse to `S₁₂`. Hence the `q → 0` data cannot distinguish\nthem, and the substrate evaluation is what separates the readings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_eq_of_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_eq_of_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L75-L80","doc":"Two indices always agree on the symmetry constant — the invariance\nstatement in the form used by the audit (\"nothing about it deforms\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant_const","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**The symmetry constant is constant.** If a family satisfies\n`S₁₂ + S₂₁ = c · S₁₁` pointwise with `S₁₁` nonvanishing, then its symmetry\nconstant equals `c` at every index — q-independence is forced by the\nsymmetry itself, not observed numerically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.symmetryConstant","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Reading R3: the symmetry constant `(S₁₂ + S₂₁) / S₁₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.valueRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.valueRatio","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L57-L58","doc":"Reading R2: the value-ratio `S₁₂ / S₁₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.rawEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesSymmetryConstant.rawEntry","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesSymmetryConstant.lean#L54-L55","doc":"Reading R1: the raw `(1,2)` entry. ","signatureChunk":0}]}